{"claims":[{"claim_text":"Republicans are proud of President Bush's historic leadership that has placed America at the forefront of helping the people of Africa, their governments, and private groups combat the catastrophic HIV/AIDS pandemic.", "claim_types":["evaluation"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The President's Emergency Plan for AIDS Relief is a five-year, $15 billion initiative, strongly backed by the Congress, to turn the tide against HIV/AIDS in the most afflicted nations of Africa and the Caribbean.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The President's Emergency Plan for AIDS Relief involves a comprehensive approach to the pandemic that includes education, abstinence, prevention, testing, treatment, and care – including advanced antiretroviral drugs.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The President's Emergency Plan for AIDS Relief follows in the finest American tradition of harnessing the power of human technology in the service of human compassion.", "claim_types":["evaluation"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The Bush Administration and the Republican Congress made fighting the HIV/AIDS pandemic a priority of U.S. foreign policy.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"America contributes to the Global Fund to Fight HIV/AIDS, Tuberculosis, and Malaria.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The United States is leading the world by example.", "claim_types":["evaluation"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"The global community must do more to halt the advance of the HIV/AIDS pandemic.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"Numerous African, American, and other international private organizations – including faith-based groups, hospitals, medical schools, corporations, and philanthropies – are helping the people of Africa as they fight HIV/AIDS with courage.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"Progress is already being seen in parts of Africa, which is proof that HIV/AIDS can be defeated.", "claim_types":["prediction"],"evidence_ids":[3]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
